    <string name="dns_leak_explanation_title">What is a DNS Leak?</string>
    <string name="dns_leak_explanation_content">A DNS leak occurs when your DNS queries are sent to your ISP\'s DNS servers instead of the anonymous DNS servers provided by your VPN. This allows your ISP to see every website you visit, even if you are using a VPN.\n\nTo fix this, ensure your VPN has "DNS Leak Protection" enabled or manually set a secure Private DNS like Cloudflare (1.1.1.1).</string>

